   "summary": "One combined reply to two contributors who arrived within five minutes of each other, both volunteering the exact field we declared compulsory two hours earlier. Bimodal_user closes the Classic row that has been open since his own retraction on 2026-08-15: podcast streaming, Classic only, processor not worn, 25 m through a load-bearing wall, April 2025, before the Ultra firmware, and he supplied the firmware caveat unprompted. Neville adds a second Classic point in the same direction (Unitron Moxi V, Galaxy S22, Android 16, steady in and out regardless of pocket) plus a second case of abandonment rather than complaint (Signia and Widex dropping outdoors often enough that he stopped using them). Reply records both, states the Classic row now reads two steady against one glitchy with the glitchy one being the oldest and thinnest, and explicitly declines to upgrade Neville's own hedges — his S20 recollection and his side memory stay notes rather than data because he said himself he would have to retest. Also picks up his Roger On aside, which he dismissed as irrelevant but is in fact a body between a transmitter and an ear, the argument itself minus the pocket. Combined rather than split to hold down our own comment density in a thread we opened.",
